🔴 Vulnerability Title

Unsigned DLL Allowing Potential Code Tampering and Execution

🔴 Description

It was observed that the application loads a DLL file (fidev.mkt1xladdin.Market1.XL.dll) that is not digitally signed, as confirmed using signature verification tools. The absence of a valid digital signature prevents verification of the file’s integrity and authenticity. This DLL is loaded by the Excel add-in during execution from a shared/network-accessible path. Lack of code signing introduces a risk of unauthorized modification without detection.

🔴 Impact
Attackers can replace or tamper with the DLL to execute malicious code
Leads to unauthorized code execution within the Excel add-in context
Potential full system compromise if malicious DLL is loaded
🔧 Mitigation
It is recommended to implement code signing for all DLLs using trusted certificates to ensure integrity and authenticity
Enforce signature validation before loading DLLs within the application
Restrict write access to DLL directories and monitor for unauthorized modifications
Implement application whitelisting to allow only trusted signed binaries
📌 PoC Steps

Step 1: Identify DLL file used by application
Step 2: Run sigcheck.exe <dll_path>
Step 3: Observe output showing “Unsigned”
Step 4: Confirm absence of digital signature

